set DT[i]="Ogre Magi has a lot of survivability but IsRealPlayer does need the ability to use his spells: an Arcane Ring might be the only item you will need all game."
set fT[i]="Use Bloodlust to help teammates chase and escape enemies and on the hero capable of dealing the most damage before major battles."
set FT[i]="Focus heroes that need to be shut down quickly with Fireblast: Hopefully they are repeatedly damaged and disabled by the effect of Multicast."
set i=i+1
set qt[19]='Ntin'
set IT[19]='h04H'
set Qt[19]='n0AA'
set RT[19]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNHeroTinker.blp"
call LQV(qt[19],"stand 2")
call LKV(qt[19],1,IT[19])
set cT[i]="Laser and Missile give Tinker massive burst damage, so it is usually a good idea to get these two skills before Rearm, your ultimate."
set CT[i]="Laser is not reduced by magic resistance or armor; you deal the number in the description exactly."
set DT[i]="You can use the active effects of items indefinitely with Rearm, which makes Boots of Travel a very powerful item for Tinker."
set fT[i]="March of the Machines can be very useful for killing creeps quickly, its large area of effect makes it useful for pushing and team fights."
set FT[i]="Level 1 of Rearm is generally enough until much later when you have the mana pool to support levels 2 and 3."
set i=i+1
set qt[20]='Emns'
set IT[20]='h04I'
set Qt[20]='n0A4'
set RT[20]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNFurion.blp"
call LQV(qt[20],"spell")
call LKV(qt[20],1.2,IT[20])
set cT[i]="Get Force of Nature early if you plan on leaving the lane to kill neutral creeps. Start with a Ring of Basilius to provide you with mana and armor."
set CT[i]="Invest points in Teleportation, it gives you the mobility to be anywhere in the map: Cancel the spell if you change your mind by clicking 'S'."
set DT[i]="Sprout can be extremely useful offensively and defensively so get at least one point in it. Higher levels increase the duration but also the mana cost."
set fT[i]="Teleportation shows allies and enemies where you intend to go, so if you want to surprise enemies, teleport where they cannot see."
set FT[i]="Wrath of Nature is a great farming tool but also a powerful nuke on enemy heroes: Hit other units nearby to deal more damage to the intended target."
set i=i+1
set qt[21]='Ogrh'
set IT[21]='h04J'
set Qt[21]='n0A3'
set RT[21]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNHellScream.blp"
call LQV(qt[21],"stand victory")
call LKV(qt[21],1,IT[21])
set cT[i]="Get Spirit Lance and Doppelwalk first because Juxtapose is better when your illusions have more health and damage."
set CT[i]="Beware of the high mana costs of your spells early game, especially for Doppelwalk, which can be an escape mechanism."
set DT[i]="Keep your opponents guessing by controlling your illusions created by Doppelwalk and Juxtapose."
set fT[i]="Your illusions are amazing for pushing later on. Focus creeps and heroes first because illusions will not create new ones when attacking buildings."
set FT[i]="Diffusal Blade and Manta Style are good choices of because they make his images much stronger by adding Agility directly."
set i=i+1
set qt[22]='Ucrl'
set IT[22]='h04K'
set Qt[22]='n0A7'
set RT[22]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNMountainGiant.blp"
call LQV(qt[22],"spell")
call LKV(qt[22],.5,IT[22])
set cT[i]="Buy items that give you at least 3 Intelligence or 39 mana in the beginning of the game so that you can use both of your spells at level 2."
set CT[i]="Avalanche and Toss should be the two spells you level first because they make you a force to be reckoned with early game."
set DT[i]="You can sometimes kill a hero outright by casting Avalanche on him, and then Tossing him on the Avalanche area of effect before the animation ends."
set fT[i]="To ensure that you Toss your desired target, isolate him by making him the only one in the area of effect. Kelen's Dagger can help you with placement."
set FT[i]="Tiny deals most of his damage through Avalanche and Toss, so the reduced attack speed from Grow is less important than the bonuses given."
set i=i+1
set qt[23]='H00K'
set IT[23]='h04L'
set Qt[23]='n0A9'
set RT[23]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNGoblinSapper.blp"
call LQV(qt[23],"stand 2")
call LKV(qt[23],1,IT[23])
set cT[i]=""
set CT[i]=""
set DT[i]=""
set fT[i]=""
set FT[i]=""
set i=i+1
set qt[24]='H00A'
set IT[24]='h04M'
set Qt[24]='n0AB'
set RT[24]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNHeroFarseer.blp"
call LQV(qt[24],"spell chain lightning")
call LKV(qt[24],1,IT[24])
set cT[i]="Chen can take control of high level neutral creeps with Holy Persuasion, making him extremely powerful at low levels even without items."
set CT[i]="Neutrals with special abilities usually are more useful, try to find out what has a disable or slow as this will be much better for attacking heroes with."
set DT[i]="When preparing to attack from the forest, start with Penitence to slow enemies. Engage enemies from the side or from behind to catch them off guard."
set fT[i]="Chen excels as a support hero, items that contribute to teammates such as Mekansm usually benefit the team more than damage items."
set FT[i]="Hand of God is really useful early on for helping allies across the map. Later, it can be used to assist with pushing or defending."
set i=i+1
set qt[25]='E005'
set IT[25]='h04N'
set Qt[25]='n0BE'
set RT[25]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNHuntress.blp"
call LQV(qt[25],"spell")
call LKV(qt[25],1,IT[25])
set cT[i]="The level of Lucent Beam determines the damage of Eclipse, making it the most important spell to get first. "
set CT[i]="Moon Glaives can be useful early if you plan to kill neutral creeps. Lifesteal items like Helm of the Dominator can help you survive against neutral creeps."
set DT[i]="Try to cast Eclipse on enemy heroes when other units are not present to maximize the damage dealt to a single target. "
set fT[i]="Later on with some attack speed, Lunar Blessing and Moon Glaives provide you with both massive damage and pushing power."
set FT[i]="You should also consider items that allow you to land Eclipse successfully and increase your carry potential in battles, such as a Black King Bar."
set i=i+1
set qt[26]='Usyl'
set IT[26]='h04O'
set Qt[26]='n0BD'
set RT[26]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNRifleman.blp"
call LQV(qt[26],"spell")
call LKV(qt[26],1.1,IT[26])
set cT[i]="Headshot will provide you with bonus damage and a short stun, making it useful for killing creeps and harassing with his incredible attack animation."
set CT[i]="Sniper usually needs to find a combination of damage, attack speed and survivability that allow him to deal significant damage but survive to do so."
set DT[i]="Sniper is very fragile so IsRealPlayer needs to maintain his range. Getting Take Aim and/or Shrapnel can help provide means of staying out of harm's way."
set fT[i]="Shrapenl can also be used for slowing opponents, pushing or defending against large waves of creeps."
set FT[i]="Try to use Assassinate to heavily damage an enemy before the fight even begins to give your team an advantage."
set i=i+1
set qt[27]='N016'
set IT[27]='h04P'
set Qt[27]='n0A8'
set RT[27]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNForestTroll.blp"
call LQV(qt[27],"stand 3")
call LKV(qt[27],1.25,IT[27])
call LKV('N02B',1.25,IT[27])
call LKV('N017',1.25,IT[27])
set cT[i]="Berserker's Rage gives Troll the option of melee combat, which gives him many powerful offensive bonuses at the cost of losing his ranged ability."
set CT[i]="roll Warlord generally does not have to worry about attack speed thanks to his set of skills, go for damage or survivability items instead."
set DT[i]="Blind will prevent your opponents from landing all their attacks, making it harder from them to harass you or kill your creeps for gold."
set fT[i]="Play defensively and fight neutral creeps too. Switch to melee form and it will allow you to have an easier time."
set FT[i]="In team battles, it is vital that you cast Blind on the enemy hero that deals the most damage as this will greatly reduce their damage output."
set i=i+1
set qt[28]='Orkn'
set IT[28]='h057'
set Qt[28]='n094'
set RT[28]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNShadowHunter.blp"
call LQV(qt[28],"stand victory")
call LKV(qt[28],1,IT[28])
set cT[i]="At least one level of Shackles is advised early on for immobilizing opponents. Remember that it is channeling so it can be interrupted or broken by yourself."
set CT[i]="Rhasta needs survivability and the mana to use his spells: Bracers, Null Talismans, Point Booster are examples of items that will help out a lot."
set DT[i]="Forked Lightning is your primary nuke and finisher due to its range and ability to hit multiple targets, so it more effective to get it earlier than later."
set fT[i]="Use Shackles and Voodoo on enemy heroes when casting Mass Serpent Ward. You can even surround an enemy completely with the right timing."
set FT[i]="Mass Serpent Wards can clear creeps quickly and deal a lot of damage over time to buildings, making them really useful for pushing and defending."
set i=i+1
set qt[29]='H008'
set IT[29]='h04U'
set Qt[29]='n0AC'
set RT[29]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNRazorManeChief.blp"
call LQV(qt[29],"stand")
call LKV(qt[29],1.5,IT[29])
set cT[i]="Rigwarl is a known for punishing heroes that attack him and surviving for long times but IsRealPlayer still needs armor, regeneration and hit points."
set CT[i]="Quill spray doesn't initially deal much damage, but the stacking effect makes it very powerful over time in battles."
set DT[i]="Sometimes one level of Goo can be enough to slow down an enemy hero early game."
set fT[i]="Rigwarl needs a fair amount of mana early-game, Ring of Basilius, Magic Stick or Bottle can boost his early offensive power immensely."
set FT[i]="You can mitigate a lot of damage if you turn your hero at the right times thanks to your passive Bristleback. Play mind games on your opponent."
set i=i+1
set qt[30]='Npbm'
set IT[30]='h053'
set Qt[30]='n0AO'
set RT[30]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNPandarenBrewmaster.blp"
call LQV(qt[30],"stand ready")
call LKV(qt[30],1,IT[30])
set cT[i]="Thunder Clap is a great skill early game but you may need to invest in regeneration items such as a Bottle, Magic Stick, Ring of Basilius or Void Stone."
set CT[i]="Drunken Haze works not only as a slow, but the miss chance reduces the damage severely for enemy heroes."
set DT[i]="Primal Split is not only for escaping: Once you master your three Pandas, Earth, Storm and Fire, you can use them offensively as well."
set fT[i]="In Primal Split form, Mangix has two useful disables that can be used against enemies: Storm's Cyclone and Earth's Hurl Boulder."
set FT[i]="Mangix usually initiates for the team, so survivability items are helpful, investing in a Kelen's Dagger to help land Thunder Clap is often a good idea."
set i=i+1
set qt[31]='H000'
set IT[31]='h04X'
set Qt[31]='n0AN'
set RT[31]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNCentaurKhan.blp"
call LQV(qt[31],"stand 3")
call LKV(qt[31],1.75,IT[31])
set cT[i]="Return should be leveled if Centaur plans to fight neutral creeps, otherwise Double Edge is more useful in the lane."
set CT[i]="Thanks to a high strength gain and the bonus strength from your ultimate, Centaur is a great at heading into battle first and receiving damage."
set DT[i]="A Hood of Defiance can prove to be just as useful as a Vanguard depending on whether the other team has a lot of magical spells."
set fT[i]="Avoid putting yourself at risk after using Double Edge. You can use it to commit suicide if you are about to die to deny opponents experience and gold."
set FT[i]="Kelen's Dagger is a great way of initiating on opponents and dealing with his slow casting animation of Stomp."
set i=i+1
set qt[32]='Naka'
set IT[32]='h052'
set Qt[32]='n0AM'
set RT[32]="ReplaceableTextures\\CommandButtons\\BTNakama.blp"
call LQV(qt[32],"stand var4")
call LKV(qt[32],1.2,IT[32])
set cT[i]="Shuriken Toss, Wind Walk and Track are much more useful than Jinada early on."
set CT[i]="You're going to need mana regen: Bottle, Ring Of Basillius and Void Stone are examples of good options. "
set DT[i]="Use Wind Walk cautiously: If you wait until the cooldown is complete before breaking out of invisibility, you can cast it again immediately afterward."
set fT[i]="Shuriken Toss and Wind Walk deal a lot of damage quickly: Search the map often for low HP heroes to hunt. "
set FT[i]="Use Track on a nearby enemy hero to allow you and your allies to outrun them. Also cast it on nearly dead heroes for bonus gold."
set i=i+1
set qt[33]='Hlgr'
set IT[33]='h04V'
set Qt[33]='n0AQ'
